✅ CODING RULES
Model Hierarchy: Route tasks intelligently. gpt-4o-mini for routing/summaries; claude-3.5-sonnet or o1 for reasoning.

Next.js 16 Caching: Use "use cache" for RAG results to prevent redundant expensive API calls.

Async Requirements: Always await params and searchParams in Page components.

Agentic Status: Show granular "Thinking" states (e.g., "Reading Reddit threads...", "Verifying citations...").

Citations: Every claim must link to a Source object with metadata (title, URL, favicon).

Strict Types: No any. Use Zod for all AI output parsing to ensure UI stability.

Action Blocks: Every research result should end with at least two "Next Step" buttons.

View Transitions: Use React 19's startTransition for smooth UI updates between agents.

🚫 NEVER DO THIS
Never use legacy middleware.ts for AI logic (use proxy.ts).

Never use unstable_cache (Next 16 has stabilized caching).

Never allow AI to output raw HTML (Use Markdown + custom components).

Never hardcode model strings; use the central /lib/ai/models.ts config.

Never block the UI during long-running agent tasks; use Server Sent Events (SSE).

🎨 UI/DESIGN (THE NEXORA AESTHETIC)
Primary Color: Violet (#7C3AED) | Accent: Cyan (#06B6D4).

Themes: Dark Mode Default (#0A0A0A).

Glassmorphism: Use backdrop-blur-md and bg-white/5 for sidebars and input fields.

Layout: Side-by-side "Canvas" view for generated docs (Artifacts).

Typography: Inter (San-serif) for UI, JetBrains Mono for Code/Agent logs.

🔌 COMPONENT PATTERN (NEXT 16 + AI)
TypeScript
// src/components/ai/ResearchResult.tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react';

interface ResearchProps {
  query: string;
}

export async function ResearchResult({ query }: ResearchProps) {
  "use cache" // Next.js 16 caching
  const data = await runAgenticSearch(query);

  return (
    <section className="space-y-4">
      <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold">{data.title}</h2>
      <div className="prose dark:prose-invert">
        {data.content}
      </div>
      <SourceList sources={data.sources} />
      <ActionFooter actions={data.suggestedActions} />
    </section>
  );
}
🔗 API ROUTE PATTERN
TypeScript
// src/app/api/chat/route.ts
import { streamText } from 'ai';
import { openrouter } from '@/lib/ai/providers';

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages, model } = await req.json();

  // 1. Validation & Rate Limiting (via proxy.ts)
  // 2. State Management (LangGraph)

  return streamText({
    model: openrouter(model),
    messages,
    temperature: 0.7,
  }).toDataStreamResponse();
}

This structure ensures your Cursor AI stays within the 2026 "Agentic Engine" boundaries. Would you like me to create the `proxy.ts` architecture to handle your multi-model routing and rate limiting?
